The 'components/hud' folder holds the React components for the opt-in compact HUD layout introduced by the 2026-09-14 custom-hud-layout plan (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-custom-hud-layout-design.md). CompactLayoutShell is the root, composing the terminal panel, vitals/room rows, the command input, chat, affects block, and two plugin-fillable widget slots (CompactWidgetSlot, backed by features/hudLayout/hudWidgetRegistry.ts and populated by plugins via PluginRuntimeApi.setHudWidget). It is a sibling to, not a replacement for, the classic LayoutShell — MainContainer.tsx picks one or the other at mount based on the hudLayout setting and viewport width, and per spec §6 the classic path must render identically to today's LayoutShell when compact is off. Styling lives in styles/hud/ (CSS modules) plus a set of plain `sa-hud-*` global classes rendered alongside each module class, which an opt-in theme (public/themes/slate-amber.css) targets instead of depending on Vite's hashed module class names.
